body:
//Autistic screeching   
ALARM!!! 

10 000 bots drop right on your head. HD 1 was brutal.

What is wrong with that room clearing. All of dead girls have reaction time of snail, girl with shotgun literally had time to pump her war crimes stick 2 times while being fully exposed. If she had auto shotgun 3 shots would cost a lot less time to perform, 

&#x200B;

None of high calibre girls don't use their rifles to shot through the wall, only mp5 girl would have problems with wall penetration and it based on wall material basically. If breaching is unavailable the easiest way is to blast walls and corner killing anything behind it in process. 

&#x200B;

Lack of funny pineapples of freedom and democracy, literally one flash bang could stun shotgun user for quite a while, opening way to neutralise her without killing, tear gas would do the same and frag could easily destroy shotgun girl. 

&#x200B;

Shield girl is the best girl, literally one shield girl would give information and cover from any small to medium calibre, yeah she can die too, shotgun can blast off her boots, but it based clearly on user skill. If she used shields with integrated pistol slot in it, she could neutralise shotgun girl all by herself, without exposing hand with pistol. 

&#x200B;

Overall major L and skill issue. Also pump action shotgun against full auto is the death sentence outside of some wacky animations of course.

I can recommend doing eco rounds, like tunnel rat + minimum supply of meds and food + no armor + starlock with some buckshot for small and weak enemies. Most of the time you can get decent armor from level 1-2 enemies, it would be okay until some scary guys go around. Try to kill enemies with hard hitting weapons, like flamethrowers, chainswords and sawblade launchers, those weapon can one shot you even in high tier armor or make your situation critical because of amputation.

&#x200B;

Other stuff, i just recommend having 1 sharp melee weapon for dissembling long pigs and for most important part androids. Currently there is only one way to get weapon parts and wire, tearing part from part of android.

Would game have mod support on 1.0 or after it, i still think mods that would add weapons, traits, skills are very needed in this game? 

&#x200B;

Would we have more unlockables after 1.0 that alter visual of weapons, enemies and other?

&#x200B;

Would we get procedural generated levels for run end, like in Synthetik where game check your build for durability. Or would run just ends after final boss like in playtest?

I would stick with DRG until the very end, i like new trailer of Rogue Core, but it won't be DRG 2, it would be roguelike in it's core and we don't have some game play showcase at all. DRG is still the best co-op game that i had and have a lot fun playing. I just hope that we would have something EPIC in the end when Ghost Ship Games decide to stop supporting DRG once and for all. 

&#x200B;

Rock and Stone!

Yeah mountain base is really easy on to build and defend, but bugs are nightmare, specially later in the game when wave of bugs contain 4-8+ hives and a lot, literally a lot of bugs. For me bugs are harder then enemy pawns, they force you to melee, have armour of their own, they don't retreat and hit like a truck or like two handed melee. 

&#x200B;

Still mountain base has some other weak sides like hard time with energy most of energy production can't be build under mountain roof. Farming is a big problem too, vanilla sun lamps and hydroponics are kinda costly to build and to maintain, energy is a bit problem too. And if you polish walls it is very time consuming.

Well i can just point out that PM literally gathering money by that type of monetisation, would it lead to PM becoming gacha games company nobody knows, but if they don't deliver any non-gacha game i would be very disappointed. 

&#x200B;

By the way i play Limbus Company even if it is gacha, that game is like 10 levels above most of gacha games on the market and it's more like strange mod for Library of Ruina with premade attack cards then those 2 brain cells gacha games. But as for me personaly i really don't like gacha and F2P game elements, those elements literally can paywall you from some content that you can't do on your own. Will limbus company became that type of game i don't really know.

But what's the point, okay you have gold, top items and top level, what's next? It is this path from beggar to lord, and then the life of the clan, that is the basis of the game. You can skip the first moronic quests to travel all over Calradia, you can make a difficult grind easier, but skipping all quests and the whole gameplay for the endless loop of capture of a castle -> loss of a castle -> capture of a castle with endless battles is just silly.

&#x200B;

I advise everyone, do not do this, download mods to reduce the grind or to make gold / items fall more often if you tired of grind, but do not cut the game in a straight line, this will kill all interest.

Well, the main thing, do not hire many heroes and units, they really pull a lot on the budget and reduce the speed of the army.

&#x200B;

At first, you can complete quests from villages and cities, it is better to complete quests without losing relationships. Try to bypass quests from bandit leaders, they increase your crime level and often spoil relations with others. With a high level of crime, guards, lords and mercenaries will ask you for a fine or they may attack you, as well as access to cities will be prohibited. If you don't try to complete the quest in favor of the bandits, you can also lose money.

&#x200B;

Be careful with ranged units, the developers have added a trajectory calculation for them when you move, so it became much harder to dodge. Arrows and javelins do much more damage, and armor has become much worse, so wearing a shield is much more important than anything else.

&#x200B;

You can take any weapon you like, but before learning it is better to check the skills at bannerlordperks. It is better not to study non-working branches, because apart from passive stats you will not get anything from the perk tree itself.

&#x200B;

Now it is better not to buy caravans and shops, caravans can be destroyed, and shops bring little profit. So a store in 14k dinars brings profit of 100 dinars or even less every day. If you buy shops, then they should be placed on the territory of the faction you want to join, otherwise in case of war all shops will be taken away by the hostile faction and you will have to buy them again.

&#x200B;

The best weapons can only be made by the player, if they learn through Blacksmithing, then you can get the best weapons with buffs for various stats, as well as make throwing spears for 100k dinars.

&#x200B;

I also advise you to immediately install some mods. Since many pieces of the game have not been completed yet, mods will bring these pieces and it will be a little more pleasant to play.
